/-!
# Reduced boundaries on surface germs, relative section modules, and zero snc discrepancy

This file collects three groups of results.

**Surface germs with reduced boundary** ([KollarFlips], (3.3.3) and Fig. 3). Let `(X, P; B)` be
a surface germ with reduced boundary over an algebraically closed field `k`.

* If `g` is a resolution of `(X, P)` whose weighted dual graph `Γ(g)` is a rational tree which
  is a chain `w_1, w_2` with `β = e_{w_1} + e_{w_2}`, and some boundary point `(C, z)` of `g` has
  `z ∈ E_{w_1} ∩ E_{w_2}`, then `(X, B)` is not log canonical near `P`. The log discrepancy
  vector vanishes, so `Θ = g⁻¹_* B + E_{w_1} + E_{w_2}` has three components with coefficient
  `1` through the closed point `z`, and `mult_z Θ ≥ 3`.
* If the minimal resolution `f` has no exceptional curves and `(X, B)` is log canonical near
  `P`, then `(X, P; B)` is of type (1), (3) or (9): `B = 0`, or `B` is a single curve smooth at
  `P`, or `mult_P B = 2` and the birational transform of `B` on the blow-up of `P` meets the
  exceptional curve in two distinct points. Here `X` is smooth, the identity is a resolution,
  and `m = mult_P B ≥ 3` is excluded by log canonicity. For `m = 2` the exceptional curve `F` of
  the blow-up has log discrepancy `0`, so log canonicity of `B' + F` forces every point of
  `F ∩ B'` to lie on one component of `B'`, smooth there and transverse to `F`; the count of
  points is `(B' · F) = mult_P B = 2`.

**Relative section modules** ([Stacks, Tag 0B5T], [Stacks, Tag 01Q3]). Let `f : Y ⟶ S` be
projective over a locally Noetherian `S`, `L` an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module some positive power
of which is generated by relative sections locally over `S`, and `F` a coherent `𝒪_Y`-module.
Over every affine open `U ⊆ S`, the module `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(f⁻¹U, F ⊗ L^{⊗ n})` is finitely
generated over the section ring `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(f⁻¹U, L^{⊗ n})`, a section `s` of `L^{⊗ a}`
acting on a section `u` of `F ⊗ L^{⊗ m}` by `u ≫ (F ◁ Stacks.GradedSections.mulMap s m)`.
Finitely many sections of one power `L^{⊗ D}` define `g : f⁻¹U ⟶ ℙᴺ` with
`g^* 𝒪(1) ≅ L^{⊗ D}`; Serre's theorem for the coherent `g_*(F ⊗ L^{⊗ r})`, carried back by the
projection formula, shows that the high degrees are generated by degree `D`, and each degree is
a finite `Γ(f⁻¹U, 𝒪)`-module.

**Zero reduced snc discrepancy.** Let `W` be a smooth variety over an algebraically closed field
of characteristic zero and `T = ∑ⱼ Tⱼ` a reduced snc divisor. A normalized divisorial
valuation `ξ` with `e_T(ξ) = 0` has its centre on a stratum of `T`, and is the monomial
valuation there whose weight is the vector `(ξ(Tⱼ))` of its orders: write the weight as
`d • α'` with `α'` primitive, pass to the snc modification adapted to `α'`, where the reduced
snc discrepancy is still zero and the centre is the new divisor `E_{α'}`, so `ξ = ord_{E_{α'}}`.
Since there are finitely many strata and a monomial valuation is determined by its stratum and
weight, there are only finitely many such `ξ` with `ξ(Tⱼ) ≤ M`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Flips.IsWeightedDualGraph.not_isLogCanonical_of_mem_support_of_isChainOrder`: a boundary
  curve through the node of a two-vertex chain is not log canonical (Fig. 3, Case (9)).
* `MMP.Flips.IsGermResolution.isSmoothScheme_of_isExceptionalCurveEnumeration`: a surface germ
  with a resolution that has no exceptional curve is smooth.
* `MMP.Flips.IsMinimalGermResolution.isFig3Type1_or_isFig3Type3_or_isFig3Type9`: log canonical
  germs with reduced boundary at a smooth point are of type (1), (3) or (9).
* `MMP.fg_sectionModule_restrict_of_isProjective`: the section module of a relatively semiample
  invertible module is generated by finitely many homogeneous elements over every affine open.
* `MMP.Fourfold.IsReducedSNCDiscrepancy.isMonomialValuationOfWeight_of_eq_zero`: a valuation of
  reduced snc discrepancy zero is monomial of weight `(ξ(Tⱼ))_{j ∈ J(ξ)}` at its centre.
* `MMP.Fourfold.isReducedSNCDiscrepancy_zero_of_isDiscrepancy`: on a smooth variety, a proper
  divisor of discrepancy `-1` over a reduced snc divisor has zero reduced snc discrepancy; so,
  by `MMP.Fourfold.isMonomialValuationOfWeight_of_isDiscrepancy_neg_one`, it is monomial at its
  centre.
* `MMP.Fourfold.finite_setOf_isReducedSNCDiscrepancy_zero`: finitely many valuations of zero
  reduced snc discrepancy have bounded orders.

## Implementation notes

* FA states the two-vertex chain lemma for the minimal resolution. The argument uses only that
  `Γ(g)` is a negative definite chain with `c_j(Γ) = 0` for all `j`, which holds for the
  weighted dual graph of any resolution, so the statement is made for an arbitrary resolution.
* Finite generation of the section module is stated as generation by a finite set `G` of
  homogeneous elements: the sums of the elements `s • g`, `g ∈ G`, `s` a homogeneous element of
  the section ring, exhaust the direct sum. For a graded module this is equivalent to being a
  finite module, and it pins the action as the multiplication `Stacks.GradedSections.mulMap`
  that defines the product of `Stacks.GradedSections.sectionRing`. The twist is written
  `F ⊗ L^{⊗ n}`, with `L^{⊗ n}` on the right, so that the action is a whiskering by `F`.
* The order `ξ(Tⱼ)` is read off a local equation `zⱼ ∈ 𝒪_{W,η}` of `Tⱼ` at the generic point
  `η` of the centre, `ξ zⱼ = exp (-ξ(Tⱼ))` in `ℤᵐ⁰`; so `ξ(Tⱼ) ≤ M` is `exp (-M) ≤ ξ zⱼ`. The
  conclusions hold for every choice of local equations, and such a choice exists.

## References

* [J. Kollár et al., *Flips and abundance for algebraic threefolds*][KollarFlips], (3.3.3),
  Fig. 3
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
-/

